  "status": "SUCCESS",
  "summary": "All checks pass: `python -m compileall app` clean, `pytest -q` → **502 passed**, and the OpenAPI document still exposes the three contract routes with the contract's exact spelling.\n\n**What I changed**\n\n*Contract alignment* — `GET /negotiation`, `POST /negotiation/routing` and `POST /negotiation/reminder` already existed here with exactly the field names, enum strings (`Sequential`/`Parallel`, `With Internal`/`With Counterparty`/`Agreed`, `Pending`/`Submitted`/`Overdue`, `Internal`/`External`) and the 404-when-not-routed behaviour the shared contract names, so no renames were needed. The work was attaching the described behaviour to them.\n\n1. **Auto Send to Counterparty (UC5)** — `app/services/lifecycle_negotiation.py`: extracted `_issue_external_link`, and `submit_review` now calls it the moment internal review completes (the last reviewer under Sequential, all reviewers under Parallel — the same \"all Submitted\" condition). The secure link and OTP are emailed to the external party via the existing `notifications.dispatch`; the tracker then reports `negotiationStatus: \"With Counterparty\"`.\n2. **OTP never in the API** — removed the `otp` field from `GenerateExternalLinkResponse`; the OTP is generated through a `_generate_otp` seam, hashed into storage, and leaves only by email. Updated the existing negotiation tests to pin that seam instead of reading the OTP off a response.\n3. **Reviewer reminders (UC5)** — the manual `POST /negotiation/reminder` now actually emails the overdue reviewer. The automatic daily variant lives in the new `app/services/scheduled_notifications.run_reviewer_reminders`: one email per day to each pending reviewer and to the owner, guarded by `negotiation_reminders` rows (`reminder_type=\"Auto\"`), stopping on submission or on Agreed.\n4. **Signature reminders (UC7)** — `run_signature_reminders` re-prompts open signers every X days (signer's frequency → tenant e-signature setting → 3), anchored on `signers.last_reminder_sent_at`, stopping on Signed/Declined/Expired or a withdrawn/declined/executed contract.\n5. **Renewal alerts (UC9)** — `run_renewal_alerts` fires at the 90/60/30 windows before the End Date and, separately, the Notice Period deadline, to the Owner and every Tenant Admin; the existing `renewal_alerts` table is the once-only guard.\n6. **Driving it** — new `app/repositories/scheduled_notifications.py` for the sweep queries, an in-process sweep task started in `app/main.py`'s lifespan (`NOTIFICATION_SWEEP_INTERVAL_SECONDS`, default 3600, `0` disables), and three new rows in the Settings → Notifications event list so each new channel honours its toggle. New `tests/test_scheduled_notifications.py` covers all four behaviours.\n\n**Constraints that shaped this:** migrations live in `alembic/`, outside the paths I may modify, so I used only tables that already exist (`negotiation_reminders`, `renewal_alerts`, `signers.last_reminder_sent_at`) and added no columns. Reading: \"the tracker shows 'Sent to counterparty'\" is the frontend's label for the contract's `negotiationStatus: \"With Counterparty\"` — I did not introduce a fourth enum value, since the contract pins that enum. Nothing in this instruction was frontend-side work.",
